# Checkout policy for bytes that are part of a contract.
#
# The resource package fixture below is compared by size and SHA-256, so a
# Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf` must not transcode its LF endings to
# CRLF: `-text` disables EOL conversion, keeping the working tree byte-identical
# to the committed (LF) blob. Existing Windows clones need a one-time
# `git checkout -- tests/fixtures/resource_equivalence/assets` after this rule
# first appears (see docs/references/windows_acceptance.md §9).
# (Shader sources are hashed after CRLF normalization in
# tools/shader_artifacts.py, so they do not need a checkout rule.)
tests/fixtures/resource_equivalence/assets/** -text
